id: hac-ckrs
title: Add typed condition evaluation and action-sequence runtime
description: "Complete the stable Home Assistant automation runtime workflow with typed one-shot condition testing, bounded condition observation, and read-only-safe action-sequence execution."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,automation,conditions,home-assistant,llm,runtime,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-06T17:05:55.428Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-06T17:05:55.428Z"
deadline: "2026-08-08T17:05:55.428Z"
assignee: unbraind
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Typed commands accept validated inline JSON and JSON files with optional variables and detailed nested help; Condition testing and bounded observation preserve Core result and template-error semantics; Action-sequence execution is blocked before network I/O whenever read-only mode is enabled; Schemas, capabilities, README, API reference, docs index, LLM guidance, and agent optimization docs remain synchronized; Focused, integration, help, wizard, all-format, live, security, PM, auto-release dry-run, and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage gates pass"
definition_of_ready: Official stable 2026.8.0 source and latest developer docs confirm contracts; live 2026.7.4 instance confirms compatibility; all-status PM and GitHub searches find no equivalent typed feature.
goal: best-agent-home-assistant-cli
objective: typed-automation-runtime
value: "Let agents validate assumptions, observe condition truth, and run reusable action sequences without raw protocol construction."
impact: "Improves safety, explainability, and prompt efficiency for automation authoring and operation."
outcome: A production-ready typed automation runtime surface with private-instance-safe evidence and no release publication.
why_now: Static validation and trigger observation are already shipped; the remaining stable runtime commands form the next coherent agent workflow.
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: 2026-08-automation-runtime
release: 2026.8.6
